		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2714&amp;p=22328#p22328"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>I would not advise at the moment that you install the UV380 or DM1701 firmware on the 2017 until we know which pins control the PA.<br>Because it may be possible to enable both Tx and Rx at the same time and damage the radio <br><br>Hopefully BD4VOW will be able to provide MCU pin mapping for this radio, becuase its not easy to reverse engineer the hardware, even if you open the radio and attempt to 'buzz' the connnections to the various chips, as it is difficult to know where the PA control transistors etc are located<br><br>We don't have a schematic for the UV380, we worked from the MD380 schematic and other information on the web about the UV380<br><br>Possibly TYT may give the pin mapping if they think it would sell more radios.</div></blockquote>Yes, I understand that it may be very risky using wrong firmware on it.<br>Spent some time today flashing it back to Retevis version 4.15 and it is probably not working 100% anymore, DMR seems to behave strange in TX.<br>Doesn't matter so much as it's a radio I don't use, the little joystick is so annoying, I prefer the RT84 even if that one has cheaper built quality.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sun Mar 05, 2023 9:35 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
