		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2714&amp;p=22302#p22302"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>OK.<br>CPS Radio Type MD2017 is the same as MD-380UV and RT-3S<br><br>Probably the MCU pin mapping for the keyboard and many other things is different.<br><br>Perhasp you can discuss with BD4VOW how to find the pin mapping on this radio, then will probably be able to support it.<br><br>BTW. Is this radio the Retevis branded version of the MD-2017, becuase BD4VOW says he will buy a MD-2017, and he can probably dissassemble the radio to try to find the pin mapping from the MCU / CPU<br>But the pin mapping differences are obviously not just the keypad <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_wink.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=";-)" title="Wink"></div></blockquote>Yes , it seems to be mostly different pin mapping compared to RT84.<br><br>I found out that the flickering display light is related to the volume control setting.<br><br>I think I found out some keys that control options and squelch and power level, and I think that most of the number keys is correct.<br><br>But it's worse that both TX and RX control pins seems completely different.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2867">SA0BUX</a> — Sat Mar 04, 2023 11:01 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
