		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2714&amp;p=22298#p22298"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div><br>I have a RT82 (GPS) which is the same radio as MD-2017 , I''m curious to test and load some OpenGD77 so I'm charging the radio now and installed the CPS X-version on my PC.<br><br>( Additionally I have the RT84 but I have lent it out for the moment, my OM friend would be very happy if it will be possibly to run OpenGD77 in the future )</div></blockquote>First test with the RT82:<br>+ Was possible to write flash with X CPS and Radio Type MD-2017 , I loaded 2023-02-27 OpenMDUV380.bin <br>+ Radio started up with the loaded software , No startup sounds , screen light is flashing randomly and radio seems to jump around in channel.<br>+ Writing a codeplug seems to work, I could write over the bad config data.<br><br>- Keyboard works randomly , not able to do any real control of the radio.<br>- No RX , was able to manipulate the squelch but no sound.<br>- It seems to go over in TX mode when I press PTT but no output.<br><br>Also tried with 2023-03-04 OpenDM1701.bin but that ones behaves similarly.</div></blockquote>OK.<br>CPS Radio Type MD2017 is the same as MD-380UV and RT-3S<br><br>Probably the MCU pin mapping for the keyboard and many other things is different.<br><br>Perhasp you can discuss with BD4VOW how to find the pin mapping on this radio, then will probably be able to support it.<br><br>BTW. Is this radio the Retevis branded version of the MD-2017, becuase BD4VOW says he will buy a MD-2017, and he can probably dissassemble the radio to try to find the pin mapping from the MCU / CPU<br>But the pin mapping differences are obviously not just the keypad <img class="smilies" src="http://localhost/opengd77/images/smilies/icon_e_wink.gif" width="15" height="17" alt=";-)" title="Wink"><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Mar 04, 2023 10:36 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
